  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Example 1 demonstrates how to find the total number of pens and pencils Raju gets, given x red boxes (each containing _______ pens) and y blue boxes (each containing _______ pencils).$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$4x, 5y$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In Example 2, the algebraic expression for the total cost incurred on fencing and sowing seeds is ` (200l + 160w + 50lw). What do these terms represent? The term 200l represents the cost of fencing along the _______ of the garden, while the term 160w represents the cost of fencing along the _______.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$length, width$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Example 3 introduces a rectangle with one side length (x cm) and the other side given by an expression. What is this second side? It is expressed as (10 – x). This makes it a(n) _______ relationship between the two sides.$qbx$, 'fill_blank'::question_type, NULL, $qbx$linear$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
