  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The slope of a line does not affect its position on the coordinate plane.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In Fig. 2.6, joining (–1, –3) and (4, 12) using a ruler would show these points lie on a straight line with slope -5/2.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The sequence in Fig. 2.4 represents a linear growth pattern.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The y-intercept of a line changes when the value of 'a' is altered, keeping 'b' fixed.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In the equation y = ax + b, if a is changed to -a while b remains constant, the slope of the line will be reversed.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The lines y = x and y = –x are parallel because they have the same slope.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If 'b' is increased in an equation like y = ax + b without changing 'a', the line shifts upwards.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For any linear equation of the form y = mx + c, if m is doubled, c will also double to maintain the same slope.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If we change the value of 'b' in an equation like y = ax + b without changing 'a', the line shifts left or right but remains parallel to the original line.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The polynomial 3x² – x + 5 is a degree 2 polynomial, not degree 3 as stated in question 1.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If we change the value of 'a' in an equation y = ax + b without changing 'b', the line's slope increases if 'a' becomes positive and decreases if 'a' becomes negative.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For each set of lines, altering the coefficient of x (changing 'a') will result in a different slope but not necessarily a change in y-intercept.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In linear equations, changing 'b' without changing 'a' does not affect the line's position relative to other lines with the same slope.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If we have two parallel lines and they intersect at (0, b), then their slopes must be different.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The graph of y = 2x + 1 intersects the y-axis at point B(0, -1).$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Changing 'a' in an equation like y = ax + b without changing 'b' results in a vertical shift upwards or downwards.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The lines y = x and y = 2x are parallel because they have the same slope.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If the value of 'b' is increased, the line shifts upwards regardless of the value of 'a'.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In an equation like y = ax + b, if a changes sign without changing b, the graph's orientation (up/down) will be flipped.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The polynomial 2x³ – x² + 4 is degree 3 as stated in question 1.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Changing 'b' in an equation like y = ax + b without changing 'a' results in a horizontal shift of the line upwards or downwards.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The lines y = x and y = –x are not parallel because they have different y-intercepts.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If we change the value of 'b' in an equation like y = ax + b without changing 'a', the line remains at a constant distance from the origin on both sides.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The lines y = 2x and y = x – 1 are parallel because they have the same slope.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The graph of y = 3x + 4 intersects the x-axis at point A(0, -4).$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In linear equations, changing 'a' without changing 'b' results in a change in the line's position relative to other lines with different slopes.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The polynomial 5x³ – 2x + 1 is degree 3 as stated in question 1.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The line y = ax always passes through point (0, a).$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The equation y = x² is not a linear polynomial.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$If the slope of a line is greater than 1, it represents a linear decay.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$For any real number k, the graph of y = (k/x) always lies in Quadrant I and III.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$The sequence generated by y = ax + b is always increasing if a > 0 and decreasing if a < 0.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$True$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '4740c507-d810-40b8-934c-5fe8df821f3c', '2dee0043-3f54-4802-8cf7-a671ddd9a1f1', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$In Fig. 2.8, the line represented by y = x has a steeper slope than y = 2x.$qbx$, 'true_false'::question_type, $qbx$[{"id":"t","text":"True"},{"id":"f","text":"False"}]$qbx$::jsonb, $qbx$False$qbx$, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-27-941Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true),
